  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Hand traps (Ash Blossom, Effect Veiler, Nibiru) are the primary disruption tools—carry at least 3 copies of Ash Blossom in any competitive deck as it counters the most common search cards in every meta.",
      "Extra Deck sequencing determines combo efficiency—most competitive combos must execute in a specific monster summon order to maintain material availability for subsequent Extra Deck plays.",
      "Gem points from ranked matches accumulate toward Secret Pack access—prioritise ranked play over solo modes for Gem income, as ranked games provide 4–8 Gems per win versus 0 from solo.",
      "Deck building should target a 40-card deck minimum—each additional card beyond 40 reduces the probability of drawing opening combo pieces; 40-card decks are statistically optimal for combo consistency.",
      "Negation effects (Solemn Judgment, Solemn Warning) are best placed face-down on Turns 2–4 rather than activated proactively—let opponents extend their combo as far as possible before negating to maximise the value of a single negation."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "手札誘発（灰流うらら、エフェクト・ヴェーラー、原始生命態ニビル）は主要な妨害ツール。灰流うらら3枚をどんな競技デッキにも持つ。全てのメタで最も一般的なサーチカードに対抗する。",
      "エクストラデッキのシーケンスがコンボ効率を決定する。ほとんどの競技コンボは後続のエクストラデッキプレイのための素材可用性を維持するために特定のモンスター召喚順序で実行しなければならない。",
      "ランクマッチからのジェムポイントはシークレットパックアクセスに蓄積される。ジェム収入のためにソロモードよりランクプレイを優先する。ランクゲームは勝利ごとに4〜8ジェムを提供し、ソロからは0。",
      "デッキ構築は最低40枚を目指す。40枚を超える各追加カードはオープニングコンボパーツをドローする確率を下げる。40枚デッキはコンボの一貫性のために統計的に最適。",
      "無効化効果（神の宣告、神の警告）はプロアクティブに発動するより2〜4ターン目に裏側で置くのが最善。単一の無効化の価値を最大化するためにネゲートする前に相手にコンボをできるだけ伸ばさせる。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Card Crafting Efficiency",
        "body": "Master Duel's crafting system (dismantling cards for CP points and using CP to craft) is the core card acquisition method for F2P players. Prioritise: never dismantle SR (Super Rare) or higher cards until you verify they will never be useful; N and R cards are safe to dismantle in bulk. The highest-value CP spend is crafting UR (Ultra Rare) staples (Ash Blossom, Pot of Prosperity) before crafting deck-specific UR engine pieces, since staples appear in multiple competitive decks."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Climbing Ranked with Budget Decks",
        "body": "Reaching Gold rank in Master Duel is achievable with budget decks (SR-only, no UR engine). Budget-viable archetypes include Branded, Exosister, and Floowandereeze—all three function with SR main-deck pieces and URs concentrated only in the Side Deck. The ranked ladder rewards CP points that fund subsequent craft purchases, creating a sustainable F2P progression loop without requiring real-money investment for competitive viability below the Diamond rank threshold."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Platinum and Master Rank Meta",
        "body": "Platinum rank and above requires running the current format's tier 1 or 2 deck with full optimal build. Track the current Master Duel meta tier list (updated weekly by the community) and only invest craft resources in decks within the top 4 archetypes. The meta shifts significantly every 2–4 months with banlist updates; maintain a 300+ UR CP buffer before the anticipated banlist date to adapt your deck if key cards get banned or limited."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not including enough hand traps in competitive decks—going to ranked with fewer than 6 hand traps (Ash Blossom, Effect Veiler, Nibiru, Impermanence, or similar) means conceding free combo turns to meta decks that run through disruption.",
      "Dismantling UR cards in bulk for CP—UR cards are expensive to re-craft (800 CP each); dismantling a UR to save 800 CP only to need it for a future meta deck wastes the same 800 CP you saved.",
      "Running a 41–50 card deck—every card over 40 reduces opening hand combo consistency by 2–3%; in combo-reliant meta decks, a 45-card deck is statistically 10% less consistent than a 40-card equivalent.",
      "Activating hand traps on the first search card rather than the combo-critical search—Ash Blossom stops one search; use it on the search that provides the combo piece that the entire sequence depends on, not the opening search that has accessible redundancy.",
      "Ignoring the Solo Mode for CP income—Solo Mode provides one-time CP rewards for completing archetypes; completing all available Solo Mode stages provides 800+ CP that funds an early competitive craft without spending ranked time."
    ],
